& [Observation] is verified routing without a first-class attention-language projection
  + route_attention currently returns the full runtime and verification records
  + procedure identity arguments content bindings account identity authority and evidence identity are present but the caller must reconstruct their ordered attention meaning

& [Intent] is one deterministic ordered AttentionFrame
  + project FOCUS BOUND ADMIT and RETURN operations only after positive runtime and evidence verification
  + retain the full runtime and verification records beside the projection
  + label caller-derived arguments as data rather than authority
  + make every operation mechanically derived from already validated fields without another model call

& [Boundary] is projection not execution
  + the frame is learned_evidence_backed_proposal and does not invoke a procedure model query or effect
  + ADMIT means the route evidence account verified and does not mean truth safety signature or permission
  + negative and infrastructure faults produce no positive AttentionFrame

& [Compatibility] preserves the one-tool input and existing result fields while adding one success-only field

& [Deferred] includes compact-only response negotiation textual prompt compilation procedure execution and signed AttentionFrames
